# Fabric Flo domain language

Fabric Flo is a phone-first app for film/TV productions to track **fabrics and their matching bags**
on set. The canonical reference is [docs/FABRIC_FLO_GLOSSARY.md](mdc:docs/FABRIC_FLO_GLOSSARY.md) —
read it before editing user-facing copy or product flows.

## Use these exact terms

- **Invite Code** — the token crew use to join a production. Never write "join code".
- **One inventory row = one fabric + matching bag pair**, tracked together under the same dynamic QR
  or rental-house label. There is no separate Fabric vs Bag UI.
- **Scan method** is `qr`, `label`, or `manual`.
- **Roles**: `admin`, `department_head`, `crew`, `viewer`.
- **Location kinds**: studio, filming location, transport truck.
- **Routes**: `/` is the marketing site, `/app` is the productions home.

## Primary flow

Coordinator signs in at `/app` -> creates a production -> creates an **Invite Code** -> shares it by
email or text -> crew enters the code -> crew scans a piece and picks a place -> it lands in the
shared log and rental inventory.

## Do not reintroduce

- "Join code" wording.
- All / Fabrics / Bags filters on Log or Inventory.
- A separate Fabric/Bag toggle or separate bag add form.
- Tracking fabric and bag as independent items with separate QRs/labels.

When changing terminology, update [docs/FABRIC_FLO_GLOSSARY.md](mdc:docs/FABRIC_FLO_GLOSSARY.md)
first, then run `npm run knowledge:export` to refresh the Claude knowledge pack.
